WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
Speaker 1: Hello, everybody. Welcome to The&nbsp;
David Pakman Show. I'm producer Pat Forde,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:08.400
filling in for David today as he continues his&nbsp;
paternity leave. Of course, yesterday we had Tdps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.960
correspondent Luke Beesley fill in for David.&nbsp;
He did an excellent job. He really set the bar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.120
high. So we'll see if I'll be able to meet that&nbsp;
threshold today for you and then the rest of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.360
week we're still trying to figure out, but I can&nbsp;
assure you that David will be back before you know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.520
it. Let's start things off today by talking&nbsp;
about day four of the January 6th hearings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.880
which took place yesterday. And the theme of the&nbsp;
day was focusing on how Trump pressured state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:36.720
level officials, mostly Republicans, mind you, to&nbsp;
overturn the election results. There was testimony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.880
from three Republican election officials,&nbsp;
Georgia Secretary of State Brad Raffensperger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.520
who at this point we're all very familiar&nbsp;
with his deputy, Gabe Sterling, and Arizona&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.080
House of Representatives speaker Rusty Bowers.&nbsp;
They were all pressured to do Trump's bidding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.720
and what I would argue was criminal influence by&nbsp;
the former president. But we'll see if the Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.120
Justice Department and Merrick Garland agree.&nbsp;
Even though these three refused to go along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:04.640
with Trump's wishes, the then president would not&nbsp;
take no for an answer, and he kept harassing them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.120
During the hearing, we learned that members of&nbsp;
Congress also tried pressuring these officials,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:14.320
including Representative Andy Biggs from Arizona,&nbsp;
who called Rusty Bowers on the morning of January&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:19.600
6th, asking him to support the certification&nbsp;
of the electoral votes. All three of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.560
people testifying, Raffensperger, Sterling and&nbsp;
Bowers, received threats from Trump supporters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.240
after they refused to go along with the plot to&nbsp;
decertify and send fake electors to various state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.560
houses who would then send the electoral votes to&nbsp;
Congress. Perhaps the most emotional part of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:40.080
day was when Rusty Bowers explained the protests&nbsp;
going on at his home as all of this was going on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.760
And even up until now, apparently protesters&nbsp;
were bothering his gravely ill daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:51.040
threatening the family, levying baseless&nbsp;
accusations against him that he's a pedophile.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.480
Let's play the moment from the hearings that was&nbsp;
perhaps the most emotional in all of yesterday.&nbsp;

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:04.160
Speaker 2: As others in the videos have mentioned,&nbsp;
we received some of my secretaries would say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:12.640
in excess of 20,000 emails and tens&nbsp;
of thousands of voicemails and texts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:20.400
which saturated our offices. And we were unable&nbsp;
to work or at least communicate that at home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:30.480
Up till even recently. It is the new pattern&nbsp;
or a pattern in our lives to worry what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:41.040
will happen on Saturdays because we have.&nbsp;
Various groups come by and. They have had.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:48.240
Video panel trucks with videos of&nbsp;
me proclaiming me to be a pedophile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.240 --> 00:03:00.800
and a pervert and a corrupt politician and blaring&nbsp;
loudspeakers in my neighborhood. And leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:08.680
literature both on my property, but arguing and&nbsp;
threatening with neighbors and with myself. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:15.920
I don't know if I should name groups, but&nbsp;
there was a one gentleman that had the three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:25.280
bars on his chest and he had a pistol. And was&nbsp;
threatening my neighbor. Not with the pistol, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:31.840
just vocally. When I saw the&nbsp;
gun, I knew I had to get close.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:49.680
And at the same time on some of these, we had a&nbsp;
daughter who was gravely ill. Who is upset. By&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:57.600
what was happening outside. And my&nbsp;
wife. That is a valiant person. Very.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:03.120
Very strong, quiet, very strong woman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:14.480
So it was disturbing. It was disturbing.
Speaker 1: Bowers went on to read an entry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.320
he wrote in his journal around this time,&nbsp;
wherein he said, quote, I do not want to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:22.640
a winner by cheating. I will not play with&nbsp;
the laws I swore allegiance to. And that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:27.280
really used to be what America was all about, that&nbsp;
Republicans and Democrats could argue and try to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:32.000
win as many votes as they could. But then once&nbsp;
you have the election and the votes are counted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.240
that's it. You tally it up. The loser concedes to&nbsp;
the winner. The winner takes office, and the loser&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:40.720
has every opportunity to run again the next time&nbsp;
if they want to. But you don't parade around the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:45.440
country saying that it was all rigged and that you&nbsp;
really won and trying to overturn election results&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:49.840
by pressuring officials and all this stuff. We had&nbsp;
this long tradition of doing it right or mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:55.360
right in this country up until Donald Trump in&nbsp;
the 2020 election. In addition to this moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:00.320
Raffensperger spoke about when Trump pressured&nbsp;
him on that famous phone call to find the, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:07.520
11,780 votes. And Sterling spoke about how&nbsp;
he in real time debunked Rudy Giuliani's lies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:13.200
about Georgia election officials supposedly&nbsp;
counting fake votes for Biden and Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:18.880
despite the fact that Sterling had debunked those&nbsp;
claims, decided to amplify the claims nonetheless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:23.760
So one would maybe look at this hearing and&nbsp;
think that, okay, maybe Trump supporters could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:29.760
convinced by this because the accounts in these&nbsp;
testimonies are coming from Republicans. So they'd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:34.320
have no agenda here, right? They're not Democrats.&nbsp;
They're not just trying to say that Biden won for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:41.040
political purposes or anything like that. However,&nbsp;
in the Trumpists eyes, these people are RINOs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:45.520
They're not true Republicans because they're&nbsp;
not true Trump supporters. So they don't count&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:51.200
right. They can be put aside and discounted.&nbsp;
So, you know, these people are largely too far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:56.080
gone. Maybe we just shouldn't try to focus too&nbsp;
much on concerning ourselves, with trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:02.240
convince them. And instead, maybe we should look&nbsp;
at these hearings as a possible way to get towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:07.520
pressuring the Biden Justice Department and&nbsp;
Attorney General Merrick Garland to press charges&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:11.760
against the former president. But given that&nbsp;
we have this long tradition of not prosecuting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:16.400
former presidents, I'm personally not going to&nbsp;
hold my breath. But it's still good to learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:20.400
all the different things that we're learning&nbsp;
about because of these January 6th hearings,

